<chapter xml:id="chapter-display" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Descriptive Statistics</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      There are, very broadly, two kinds of statistics: descriptive
      statistics and inferencetial statistic. The technical part of
      the course starts with descriptive statistics. The problem here
      is the opacity of a data set. A data set, particularly a large
      one, is just a huge collection of categories, values and
      numbers. It's usually imposslbe to look at a data set and see
      much of anything. Descriptive statistics is a set of method to
      display the information in dataset. The five outcomes in this
      section present various ways to present and visualize different
      kinds of variables in differnet kinds of datasets. 
    </p>
  </introduction>

